// Watchdog for the "D-Code bug": when a per-room-member profile fetch wedges
// (state 6 payload-rejected, or a >15s state-2 stall), force the slot back to
// idle so the game's own retry path re-fetches. See docs/Research/DCodeNetworkStallBug.md.
SETTING(bool, dcodeAutoRecover, "DCodeAutoRecover", "1");
// TEST ONLY: sabotage the first in-flight profile fetch after launch (corrupts
// the receive buffer so the game's checksum rejects it) to exercise the state-6
// wedge + auto-recovery end-to-end. Fires once per launch while set to 1.
SETTING(bool, dcodeForceFailureOnce, "DCodeForceFailureOnce", "0");
// Spectator desync candidate fix: when the spectator's SynchronizeInput fails
// (input not yet received), always stall the frame instead of letting the game
// advance the simulation with zeroed inputs (the desync mechanism at VA
// 0x4E60D5). Log-only diagnostics run regardless; this flips the actual fix.
// See docs/Research/SpectatorDesyncInvestigation.md.
SETTING(bool, spectatorSyncFailStall, "SpectatorSyncFailStall", "0");
// Keep the last N sessions' DEBUG.txt files in BBCF_IM\DebugHistory (rotated at
// launch). 0 = old behavior, DEBUG.txt is overwritten every launch.
SETTING(int, debugLogSessionHistory, "DebugLogSessionHistory", "10");
